{"availability":"available","full":"onepagezen/ob-frontend","name":"ob-frontend","description":"ob-frontend is a headless WordPress starter theme built with Gatsby.","category":"Other","language":"JavaScript","stars":8,"forks":4,"created":"2020-09-22T01:57:47Z","updated":"2020-12-27T18:48:41Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"","topics":["blog","bloomer","cloud-computing","gatsby","gatsby-plugin","gatsby-wordpress","gatsby-wordpress-theme","google-cloud-platform","graphql","headless-cms","headless-wordpress","jamstack","mailchimp","netlify","ob-frontend","react","static","wordpress","wordpress-backend","wordpress-frontend"],"demo":"https://ob-frontend.netlify.app/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T09:12:18.135Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-06T09:12:18.135Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-06T09:12:18.135Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T09:12:18.135Z","stars":8,"forks":4}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["ob-frontend is a headless WordPress starter theme built with Gatsby.","ob-frontend is a modern implementation of the WordPress frontend as a single-page application (SPA). This template, developed and packaged as a Gatsby starter, is a solution for developers looking for the ease-of-use and flexibility that comes with using WordPress as a CMS, paired with the familiar development experience and modern UI features of a React/GraphQL implementation. The ob-frontend Gatsby Starter attempts to closely mirror many of the core features and functionality of the familiar WordPress UI, such as nested comments, post sidebar layout, and a mailing list widget."],"features":["Post, page, and comment list functionality supported by Apollo client.","Modern UI powered by Bloomer React components for Bulma.","Feature-rich design capabilities supported by Sass.","Dynamic support for changing theme colors.","Support for featured posts on homepage."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/onepagezen/ob-frontend/bl